  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-a6dbdf61-7fff-ec37-2714-134e91e7b2d4&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-0be9b177-7fff-5369-2179-b2ba9da8f044&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;&quot;&gt;The development, by reason of its inappropriate scale, substandard design, and materials, results in a visually intrusive, incongruous and harmful addition to the streetscape. The development fails to respect the character and appearance of the area and is contrary to Policy LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033, Policy D3 (Optimising Site Capacity through the Design-Led Approach) of the London Plan and Hackney Shopfronts SPD.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-efa40e39-7fff-5953-8015-aa16967f2f37&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;The development, by reason of its&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt; inappropriate scale and location upon the public highway, would detrimentally restrict pedestrian movement within the vicinity of the site and adversely impact public safety for users of the surrounding public realm. The proposal fails to comply with Policies PP1 (Public Realm) LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character) LP2 (Amenity), LP42 (Walking and Cycling),&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt; LP43 (Transport and Development) of the Hackney Local Plan (2020) and Policy D8 (Public Realm) of the London Plan (2021). &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
